      "title": "High Dividend Landscape: Yield vs. Sustainability",
      "type": "context",
      "group": "overview",
      "content": "With 10-year Treasuries yielding ~4.8%, investors hunting for income are looking at **PFE (6.20%)**, **VZ (5.52%)**, **T (4.26%)**, **PEP (4.22%)**, and **NVO (4.13%)** — all beating the risk-free rate. The key tension: **PFE's headline 6.2% yield masks a fragile payout** (dividend/earnings ratio of 226%), while **T and VZ offer more sustainable telecom-style payouts** with stronger balance sheets. **VZ** stands out as the only **Buy-rated** name with both a 5.5% yield and +32.67% YTD performance."
